            "prompt": "Use case: precise-object-edit. Image1 is a new hand-drawn record-shop game background; preserve it EXACTLY, with only this one correction based on original Image2. Restore the permanent dark illustrated vinyl album sleeves/record covers lying on the FAR RIGHT foreground yellow counter beyond the lava lamp, partly cropped by the right edge, as visible in image2 lower-right. This is a small shallow flat stack with an illustrated band/collage cover, lying in the counter perspective; NOT a raised vertical display, no new textual clues. It should occupy roughly source640-coordinate x570..640,y320..417, scaled to1448x1086canvas, behind/alongside the lamp on right. Render covers freshly in same clean dark contour matte2D style (no photocopy of oldpixels). Keep every other pixel, cabinet, lamp, turntable, stool, mural, shelf, window, guitar, bodyemptyfloor and perspective as close toimage1 as possible. No actors, no UI or blankstrip, no extra labels, preserve full4:3.",
            "review": "Fixes-78 (Audit 76 'disk-part2 missing_vs_original'): the loose ruled sheet from the original disk1 background is painted back on the floor in front of the left cabinet (procedural drawing, builds/fixes-78/record-shop/tools/lined_sheet.py); every other pixel unchanged. Fixes-81 (Audit 76 '[HIGH] story 1 Ö²Â· disk-part2 Ö²Â· legacy_art_leak'): the LP stack on the yellow counter at the lower right (bg px x 1231-1447, y 682-897), whose three covers reproduced the Legacy album art, is redrawn with new original cover designs (builds/art-80/gen/album-covers-v1-fixed.png): MARMALADE SKY on top, VELVET MORNING (title column) in the middle, LIGHT SHOW (blue) at the bottom, each mapped onto the full perspective quad of the cover it replaces (reconstructed from the old covers' visible edges in the counter plane), with redrawn light sleeve edges, ink outlines, contact shadows and the turntable's shadow strip; the fourth sleeve's edge at the right border is redrawn as a plain dark sleeve; the lava lamp's cel-shaded cast shadow continues from the counter over the top cover with the counter's steps (penumbra x0.82, core x0.666) and ends there in a rounded tip at the first bandsman's hands, the same design spot in both cameras (fixes-81/record-covers/tools/make_covers.py). Lava lamp, turntable and counter untouched; every pixel outside that area unchanged."
