        "tool": "procedural (builds/fixes-80/paper-desk-newspaper/tools): invented 1967 broadsheet plate set from Windows fonts, physical sheet model on the measured desk top, supersampled inverse mapping, ink contour, contact shadow",
        "sha256": "456454aa536d5f0246d53737950b9c3676ab32daf2ecc4a081dd5236dec75e02",
        "review": "Audit 76 [LOW] story 1 paper-part2 missing_vs_original: the open tan newspaper the original painted across the left end of Nika's desk (paper1/paper2) is redrawn in the Modern style as a separate room-dressing prop for the wide newspaper office (paper1/paper2: wide-offhook-v1.png, wide-handset-v1.png; also the papern 'reach' cinematic, which reuses wide-handset-v1.png). No hotspot (the original had none). Drawn by modern_paper_scene.gd over the camera image of its legacy background members at z_index 30, under Nika (31); never resolved as a background or channel sprite (scope role room_decor).",
        "previous_sha256": "11550e8350ebe07d2e70684ea5039ac1ebf1604aeb118ee89788cf6697261bca",
        "retouch": "Fixes-84 small-art-fixes: rebuilt with the fixes-80 tools. Dateline FRIDAY, MAY 19, 1967 / NO. 139, agreeing with the game's Golden Gate newspaper clue (Np_z, May 1967); the lower-half head BRIDGE TOLL VOTE SET FOR TUESDAY set at 32 px so the papern close-up's frame edge falls in the word space before SET (it read 'TE SET FOR TUESDAY'); warm shading ramp: shadowed paper gains saturation like the room's yellowed newsprint (hanging flap median (140, 122, 94) -> (166, 130, 82)). Size, scene_rect, frames, alpha and .import identical to the fixes-80 sprite 11550e83.",
